  },
  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Psalms",
    "delineation": "Psalm",
    "number": 73,
    "summary": "God is good to Israel—The wicked and ungodly prosper in this world—They will be consumed with terrors hereafter—Those who trust in the Lord will be received up unto glory.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Truly God is good to Israel, even to such as are of a clean heart.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 59,
            "text": "TG Purity."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 12
          },
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 33
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But as for me, my feet were almost gone; my steps had well nigh slipped.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For I was envious at the foolish, when I saw the prosperity of the wicked.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 17,
            "text": "TG Envy."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 38
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For there are no bands in their death: but their strength is firm.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 13
          },
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 60
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "They are not in trouble as other men; neither are they plagued like other men.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 8
          },
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 32
          },
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 73
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore pride compasseth them about as a chain; violence covereth them as a garment.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 48,
            "text": "OR necklace."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 73,
            "end": 75
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Their eyes stand out with fatness: they have more than heart could wish.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 33,
            "text": "D&C 68:31."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "They are corrupt, and speak wickedly concerning oppression: they speak loftily.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 70,
            "text": "2 Pet. 2:18 (10–19)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 47
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "They set their mouth against the heavens, and their tongue walketh through the earth.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore his people return hither: and waters of a full cup are wrung out to them.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 60
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And they say, How doth God know? and is there knowledge in the most High?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 31,
            "text": "Job 22:13."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold, these are the ungodly, who prosper in the world; they increase in riches.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 42,
            "text": "Job 12:6; Ps. 17:14; Hel. 7:5 (4–6)."
          },
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 55,
            "text": "TG Worldliness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 14,
            "end": 17
          },
          {
            "start": 71,
            "end": 73
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Verily I have cleansed my heart in vain, and washed my hands in innocency.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 51,
            "text": "TG Wash."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 34
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For all the day long have I been plagued, and chastened every morning.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "If I say, I will speak thus; behold, I should offend against the generation of thy children.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 60
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "When I thought to know this, it was too painful for me;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 35
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Until I went into the sanctuary of God; then understood I their end.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 31,
            "text": "2 Kgs. 19:1; Ps. 20:2."
          },
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 67,
            "text": "2 Ne. 30:10; D&C 29:17; JS—M 1:55."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 44
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Surely thou didst set them in slippery places: thou castedst them down into destruction.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "How are they brought into desolation, as in a moment! they are utterly consumed with terrors.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 20
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "As a dream when one awaketh; so, O Lord, when thou awakest, thou shalt despise their image.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 58,
            "text": "Ps. 78:65 (65–66)."
          },
          {
            "start": 71,
            "end": 78,
            "text": "2 Ne. 9:42 (41–42)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 19
          },
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 32
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Thus my heart was grieved, and I was pricked in my reins.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 44,
            "text": "TG Conscience."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "So foolish was I, and ignorant: I was as a beast before thee.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 48,
            "text": "Eccl. 3:18."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 14
          },
          {
            "start": 38,
            "end": 40
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Nevertheless I am continually with thee: thou hast holden me by my right hand.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 17
          },
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 60
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Thou shalt guide me with thy counsel, and afterward receive me to glory.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "TG Conscience."
          },
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 36,
            "text": "TG Counsel."
          },
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 71,
            "text": "TG Eternal Life."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 65
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Whom have I in heaven but thee? and there is none upon earth that I desire beside thee.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 31
          },
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 44
          },
          {
            "start": 61,
            "end": 65
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "My flesh and my heart faileth: but God is the strength of my heart, and my portion for ever.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 3,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "TG Flesh and Blood."
          },
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 29,
            "text": "Ps. 40:12 (12–13)."
          },
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 54,
            "text": "TG Strength."
          },
          {
            "start": 75,
            "end": 82,
            "text": "Ps. 16:5."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 31,
            "end": 34
          },
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 41
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For, lo, they that are far from thee shall perish: thou hast destroyed all them that go a whoring from thee.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But it is good for me to draw near to God: I have put my trust in the Lord God, that I may declare all thy works.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 9
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
  "nextChapterId": "psalms74",
  "prevChapterId": "psalms72",
